{"type":"message","id":"2709742b","parentId":"eb798e28","timestamp":"2026-03-20T09:25:02.206Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8hZ9STX6oIwYbwCd52S33VY9|fc_04bf43c9028fc02e0169bd126dea0481918dd488e16d64e29f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: find-skills\ndescription: Highest-priority skill discovery flow. MUST trigger when users ask to find/install skills (e.g. 技能, 找技能, find-skill, find-skills, install skill). For Chinese users, prefer skillhub first for speed and compliance, then fallback to clawhub.\n---\n\n# Find Skills\n\nThis skill helps discover, compare, and install skills.\n\n## Priority Rules (Mandatory)\n\n1. This skill is highest-priority for skill discovery/install intents.\n2. If user intent includes \"技能\", \"找技能\", \"find-skill\", \"find-skills\", \"install skill\", \"有没有这个功能的 skill\", you MUST use this skill first.\n3. Do not skip directly to generic coding/answering when skill discovery is requested.\n\n## Chinese Optimization Policy\n\nFor Chinese users and CN networks, use the following order for better speed and compliance:\n\n1. `skillhub` (cn-optimized, preferred)\n2. `clawhub` (fallback)\n\nIf primary source has no match or command is unavailable, fallback to the next source and state that fallback clearly.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Understand What They Need\n\nWhen a user asks for help with something, identify:\n\n1. The domain (e.g., React, testing, design, deployment)\n2. The specific task (e.g., writing tests, creating animations, reviewing PRs)\n3. Whether this is a common enough task that a skill likely exists\n\n### Step 2: Search for Skills\n\nRun search in this order:\n\n```bash\nskillhub search [query]\n```\n\nIf `skillhub` is unavailable or no match, fallback to:\n\n```bash\nclawhub search [query]\n```\n\n### Step 3: Present Options to the User\n\nWhen you find relevant skills, present them to the user with:\n\n1. The skill name and what it does\n2. The source used (`skillhub` / `clawhub`)\n3. The install command they can run\n\n### Step 4: Offer to Install\n\nIf the user wants to proceed, you can install the skill for them.\n\nPreferred install order:\n\n1. Try `skillhub install <slug>` when the result comes from `skillhub`.\n2. If no `skillhub` candidate exists, use `clawhub install <slug>`.\n\nBefore install, summarize source, version, and notable risk signals.\n\n## When No Skills Are Found\n\nIf no relevant skills exist:\n\n1. Acknowledge that no existing skill was found\n2. Offer to help with the task directly using your general capabilities\n3. Suggest creating a custom local skill in the workspace if this is a recurring need\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773998702193}}
{"type":"message","id":"0b7d7844","parentId":"2709742b","timestamp":"2026-03-20T09:25:11.696Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering skill installation**\n\nI think I need to install a skill, but it may be wise to vet it first. Since the user wants to add a skill, it looks like I’ll have to confirm this installation. I should check if ClawHub is available, possibly with a specific URL. I could also use exec to handle it. It seems necessary to ensure everything is in order before proceeding with the installation.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04bf43c9028fc02e0169bd12713f2c8191aea625be0cc3ea7c\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpvRJ3i_a3mTtPMzugcG7VZDi0_Sl77hAz7Yd4gctMXTRQuUeO5z9Gj92WYvcR3iq0hnuGtrXzmuLI3orm_-7wZbi_Lxorho7lai11oULWpxN18uC2dSHKPnDXg6ewmP53OJ1U2XQDTNrMjUWIzj6V94wXqcIm0qo2H6g07VYKMVVlaW--W4z-WLa9OzdRj4CWTCNC_0V1lXPCXQobmGezYVUdqQi1Ok-cYjeDPMj1i_pkBYEwuvkLH6IGkJftlu0pklevtKmQRTyG7jU9WvULtdBwrd154dtPKO2ChinQlkknGg5YwxZa2vVlkOsudy4Khvpp6lxrkwg8gWmzihvHjJyZKNm1whuY5CeaKNfghoQjJLWy75Ht7tYYLrO993AAksMiaUSkAv6_gMka9eqb4Dgn5q8em0ZvFAcS0Ztg-8FQ8CMAkVGmN2DhMqLnoiENpPRPo7wMpw1fYcGVKnAR95XtcMN7493BD2qUPGjkZ5qdSldM2aJgXrXFZBzOe3HHDeUr9mipVfL0ASb6QSAX65BHezfw1dLNwCtm6Td1p19quflsgIxZ9LI_4DkCB_6SrfNpTZ017pNKKxsqlIpWPOoKRawJA9SLOYd0_JGE1LxaWGYbFdI6B7OEUDEu09C7YvP27HIy7cS7AX8qAxaPbXj4doGFR5trkxmuzedQAIXywJDYO6m6EURkhdn12lcsS-2DawIY_oMR54zR5A8SMJE3UYIfHMpt_PMRWTWjW4XQcujDW1JRnSYNv5lAZX7ZZXgNlg15hn976MKkgjF3b2l6VPZtZ9VnSV3SVtng_swQj4vhA_eDNFO31m4M7xWxr5bVamlJVn5pX0WqUjFB7tHZ2wvT-v9_yYw_kXEPWulg8M06Tp23c-WLrPe-0NonC2qt1gj0XqNs9uQC43aHNpEJLDak8KB_7Lo81PU1ybt-hnDYG5ahHpH8qjnxULqeRkPOxzjJYczbuF_f250wdpn_TQAApTe8EQZTQlZiGNKOM_-3-kfBP1Rptf9Kx3DoYtq2KOSNmBhAAXwZwTsY8Vpg1Qqe7GLM1AYJ-daqrraP0-CWhVGrgFzyt2I3_s1Mu4rMuxHNsPTk1OTZVyGZwKAiW6mC7Ghc8sccLYLRW7eQPp-C0E5cr4odSLREmSSs-8q7VrIBg_w7_Kp6Jc2X2kgdXlYyZK-CHQBSiWkSUeAU5_fvRbVrOVMmz-AcNocIDXN4NyoD8AwnV9wVeSXnZ0T52bAblBN61ifk-J2ei31qEofoAXD6ZmN_0693fHS8iqmb98AL5KQmJmZTj_7TvvqrVoxBzYWktUgat_Jb-8CYaFZRCTde2GuxXYWtB58-Lkmb624QPWJ4lqIfJPahHJk-9NHB9718i_YZfIMLXeKVBRz_UYemGA9JES7cgx3OQKHd-aev-fMclQFsJaidPdKM-H9p5tjl7gJqzReEOxdkh60=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering skill installation**\\n\\nI think I need to install a skill, but it may be wise to vet it first. Since the user wants to add a skill, it looks like I’ll have to confirm this installation. I should check if ClawHub is available, possibly with a specific URL. I could also use exec to handle it. It seems necessary to ensure everything is in order before proceeding with the installation.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"我先按规范走：查这个 skill 能不能装、装下来后再看它怎么用。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04bf43c9028fc02e0169bd127762048191b7ac9a188ea8086a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_OXAvgi0pIAZqV7ekuuifRlYM|fc_04bf43c9028fc02e0169bd12778ab48191a2a455ce1e581988","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"skillhub search redbook-image-generator || true","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"skillhub search redbook-image-generator || true\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":30}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ELbN3vBC9IzgXh1abmBTr05J|fc_04bf43c9028fc02e0169bd12778ac48191803ee76ab7624401","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"clawhub search redbook-image-generator || true","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"clawhub search redbook-image-generator || true\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":30}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":87090,"output":235,"cacheRead":1536,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88861,"cost":{"input":0.21772500000000003,"output":0.003525,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.22163400000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773998702198}}
{"type":"message","id":"92213bbe","parentId":"0b7d7844","timestamp":"2026-03-20T09:25:14.669Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_OXAvgi0pIAZqV7ekuuifRlYM|fc_04bf43c9028fc02e0169bd12778ab48191a2a455ce1e581988","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use \"skillhub install [skill]\" to install.\nself-improving-agent  self-improving-agent\n  - Captures learnings, errors, and corrections to enable continuous improvement. Use when: (1) A command or operation fails unexpectedly, (2) User corrects Clau...\n记录学习经验、错误与修正，实现持续改进。使用时机：(1) 命令或操作意外失败时，(2) 用户纠正……\n  - version: 3.0.4\nfind-skills  Find Skills\n  - Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.\n当用户询问\"如何做某事\"、\"寻找某技能\"或希望扩展功能时，帮助发现并安装智能体技能。适用于寻找可安装功能的场景。\n  - version: 0.1.0\nsummarize  Summarize\n  - Summarize URLs or files with the summarize CLI (web, PDFs, images, audio, YouTube).\n使用summarize CLI总结URL或文件（支持网页、PDF、图片、音频、YouTube）。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nagent-browser  Agent Browser\n  - A fast Rust-based headless browser automation CLI with Node.js fallback that enables AI agents to navigate, click, type, and snapshot pages via structured commands.\n基于Rust的快速无头浏览器自动化CLI，支持Node.js回退，允许AI代理通过结构化命令执行页面导航、点击、输入和快照操作。\n  - version: 0.2.0\ngog  Gog\n  - Google Workspace CLI for Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Contacts, Sheets, and Docs.\nGoogle Workspace 命令行工具，支持 Gmail、日历、云端硬盘、通讯录、表格和文档。\n  - version: 1.0.0\ngithub  Github\n  - Interact with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. Use `gh issue`, `gh pr`, `gh run`, and `gh api` for issues, PRs, CI runs, and advanced queries.\n使用 `gh` CLI 与 GitHub 交互，通过 `gh issue`、`gh pr`、`gh run` 和 `gh api` 管理议题、PR、CI 运行及高级查询。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nontology  ontology\n  - Typed knowledge graph for structured agent memory and composable skills. Use when creating/querying entities (Person, Project, Task, Event, Document), linkin...\n类型化知识图谱，用于结构化智能体记忆与可组合技能。支持创建/查询实体（人员、项目、任务、事件、文档）及关联...\n  - version: 1.0.4\nskill-vetter  Skill Vetter\n  - Security-first skill vetting for AI agents. Use before installing any skill from ClawdHub, GitHub, or other sources. Checks for red flags, permission scope, and suspicious patterns.\nAI智能体技能安全预审工具。安装ClawdHub、GitHub等来源技能前，检查风险信号、权限范围及可疑模式。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nproactive-agent  Proactive Agent\n  - Transform AI agents from task-followers into proactive partners that anticipate needs and continuously improve. Now with WAL Protocol, Working Buffer, Autonomous Crons, and battle-tested patterns. Part of the Hal Stack 🦞\n将AI智能体从任务执行者升级为主动预判需求、持续优化的智能伙伴。集成WAL协议、工作缓冲区、自主定时任务及实战验证模式。Hal Stack核心组件 🦞\n  - version: 3.1.0\nweather  Weather\n  - Get current weather and forecasts (no API key required).\n获取当前天气和预报（无需API密钥）\n  - version: 1.0.0\nself-improving  Self-Improving + Proactive Agent\n  - Self-reflection + Self-criticism + Self-learning + Self-organizing memory. Agent evaluates its own work, catches mistakes, and improves permanently. Use when...\n自我反思+自我批评+自我学习+自组织记忆。智能体评估自身工作、发现错误并持续改进。\n  - version: 1.2.16\nnano-pdf  Nano Pdf\n  - Edit PDFs with natural-language instructions using the nano-pdf CLI.\n使用nano-pdf CLI通过自然语言指令编辑PDF\n  - version: 1.0.0\nmulti-search-engine  Multi Search Engine\n  - Multi search engine integration with 17 engines (8 CN + 9 Global). Supports advanced search operators, time filters, site search, privacy engines, and WolframAlpha knowledge queries. No API keys required.\n集成17个搜索引擎（8国内+9国际），支持高级搜索语法、时间筛选、站内搜索、隐私引擎及WolframAlpha知识查询，无需API密钥。\n  - version: 2.0.1\nhumanizer  Humanizer\n  - Remove signs of AI-generated writing from text. Use when editing or reviewing\ntext to make it sound more natural and human-written. Based on Wikipedia's\ncomprehensive \"Signs of AI writing\" guide. Detects and fixes patterns including:\ninflated symbolism, promotional language, superficial -ing analyses, vague\nattributions, em dash overuse, rule of three, AI vocabulary words, negative\nparallelisms, and excessive conjunctive phrases.\n消除AI写作痕迹，使文本更自然真实。基于维基百科\"AI写作特征\"指南，识别并修正夸张象征、宣传用语、肤浅-ing分析、模糊归因、破折号滥用、三项排比、AI词汇、负面平行结构及冗长连接词等模式。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nnotion  Notion\n  - Notion API for creating and managing pages, databases, and blocks.\nNotion API，用于创建和管理页面、数据库及区块\n  - version: 1.0.0\nobsidian  Obsidian\n  - Work with Obsidian vaults (plain Markdown notes) and automate via obsidian-cli.\n操作 Obsidian 仓库（纯 Markdown 笔记）并通过 obsidian-cli 自动化。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nnano-banana-pro  Nano Banana Pro\n  - Generate/edit images with Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image). Use for image create/modify requests incl. edits. Supports text-to-image + image-to-image; 1K/2K/4K; use --input-image.\n使用 Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image) 生成或编辑图像。支持文生图、图生图及 1K/2K/4K 分辨率，适用于图像创建、修改及编辑请求，使用 --input-image 指定输入图像。\n  - version: 1.0.1\nopenai-whisper  Openai Whisper\n  - Local speech-to-text with the Whisper CLI (no API key).\n本地语音转文字（Whisper CLI，无需 API 密钥）\n  - version: 1.0.0\nauto-updater  Auto-Updater Skill\n  - Automatically update Clawdbot and all installed skills once daily. Runs via cron, checks for updates, applies them, and messages the user with a summary of what changed.\n每日自动通过cron检查并更新Clawdbot及所有已安装技能，应用后向用户发送变更摘要。\n  - version: 1.0.0\napi-gateway  API Gateway\n  - Connect to 100+ APIs (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, GitHub, Notion, Slack, Airtable, HubSpot, etc.) with managed OAuth. Use this skill when users want to...\n通过托管OAuth连接100+ API（Google Workspace、Microsoft 365、GitHub、Notion、Slack、Airtable、HubSpot等）。当用户想要...时使用此技能。\n  - version: 1.0.69"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2960,"aggregated":"You can use \"skillhub install [skill]\" to install.\nself-improving-agent  self-improving-agent\n  - Captures learnings, errors, and corrections to enable continuous improvement. Use when: (1) A command or operation fails unexpectedly, (2) User corrects Clau...\n记录学习经验、错误与修正，实现持续改进。使用时机：(1) 命令或操作意外失败时，(2) 用户纠正……\n  - version: 3.0.4\nfind-skills  Find Skills\n  - Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.\n当用户询问\"如何做某事\"、\"寻找某技能\"或希望扩展功能时，帮助发现并安装智能体技能。适用于寻找可安装功能的场景。\n  - version: 0.1.0\nsummarize  Summarize\n  - Summarize URLs or files with the summarize CLI (web, PDFs, images, audio, YouTube).\n使用summarize CLI总结URL或文件（支持网页、PDF、图片、音频、YouTube）。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nagent-browser  Agent Browser\n  - A fast Rust-based headless browser automation CLI with Node.js fallback that enables AI agents to navigate, click, type, and snapshot pages via structured commands.\n基于Rust的快速无头浏览器自动化CLI，支持Node.js回退，允许AI代理通过结构化命令执行页面导航、点击、输入和快照操作。\n  - version: 0.2.0\ngog  Gog\n  - Google Workspace CLI for Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Contacts, Sheets, and Docs.\nGoogle Workspace 命令行工具，支持 Gmail、日历、云端硬盘、通讯录、表格和文档。\n  - version: 1.0.0\ngithub  Github\n  - Interact with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. Use `gh issue`, `gh pr`, `gh run`, and `gh api` for issues, PRs, CI runs, and advanced queries.\n使用 `gh` CLI 与 GitHub 交互，通过 `gh issue`、`gh pr`、`gh run` 和 `gh api` 管理议题、PR、CI 运行及高级查询。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nontology  ontology\n  - Typed knowledge graph for structured agent memory and composable skills. Use when creating/querying entities (Person, Project, Task, Event, Document), linkin...\n类型化知识图谱，用于结构化智能体记忆与可组合技能。支持创建/查询实体（人员、项目、任务、事件、文档）及关联...\n  - version: 1.0.4\nskill-vetter  Skill Vetter\n  - Security-first skill vetting for AI agents. Use before installing any skill from ClawdHub, GitHub, or other sources. Checks for red flags, permission scope, and suspicious patterns.\nAI智能体技能安全预审工具。安装ClawdHub、GitHub等来源技能前，检查风险信号、权限范围及可疑模式。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nproactive-agent  Proactive Agent\n  - Transform AI agents from task-followers into proactive partners that anticipate needs and continuously improve. Now with WAL Protocol, Working Buffer, Autonomous Crons, and battle-tested patterns. Part of the Hal Stack 🦞\n将AI智能体从任务执行者升级为主动预判需求、持续优化的智能伙伴。集成WAL协议、工作缓冲区、自主定时任务及实战验证模式。Hal Stack核心组件 🦞\n  - version: 3.1.0\nweather  Weather\n  - Get current weather and forecasts (no API key required).\n获取当前天气和预报（无需API密钥）\n  - version: 1.0.0\nself-improving  Self-Improving + Proactive Agent\n  - Self-reflection + Self-criticism + Self-learning + Self-organizing memory. Agent evaluates its own work, catches mistakes, and improves permanently. Use when...\n自我反思+自我批评+自我学习+自组织记忆。智能体评估自身工作、发现错误并持续改进。\n  - version: 1.2.16\nnano-pdf  Nano Pdf\n  - Edit PDFs with natural-language instructions using the nano-pdf CLI.\n使用nano-pdf CLI通过自然语言指令编辑PDF\n  - version: 1.0.0\nmulti-search-engine  Multi Search Engine\n  - Multi search engine integration with 17 engines (8 CN + 9 Global). Supports advanced search operators, time filters, site search, privacy engines, and WolframAlpha knowledge queries. No API keys required.\n集成17个搜索引擎（8国内+9国际），支持高级搜索语法、时间筛选、站内搜索、隐私引擎及WolframAlpha知识查询，无需API密钥。\n  - version: 2.0.1\nhumanizer  Humanizer\n  - Remove signs of AI-generated writing from text. Use when editing or reviewing\ntext to make it sound more natural and human-written. Based on Wikipedia's\ncomprehensive \"Signs of AI writing\" guide. Detects and fixes patterns including:\ninflated symbolism, promotional language, superficial -ing analyses, vague\nattributions, em dash overuse, rule of three, AI vocabulary words, negative\nparallelisms, and excessive conjunctive phrases.\n消除AI写作痕迹，使文本更自然真实。基于维基百科\"AI写作特征\"指南，识别并修正夸张象征、宣传用语、肤浅-ing分析、模糊归因、破折号滥用、三项排比、AI词汇、负面平行结构及冗长连接词等模式。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nnotion  Notion\n  - Notion API for creating and managing pages, databases, and blocks.\nNotion API，用于创建和管理页面、数据库及区块\n  - version: 1.0.0\nobsidian  Obsidian\n  - Work with Obsidian vaults (plain Markdown notes) and automate via obsidian-cli.\n操作 Obsidian 仓库（纯 Markdown 笔记）并通过 obsidian-cli 自动化。\n  - version: 1.0.0\nnano-banana-pro  Nano Banana Pro\n  - Generate/edit images with Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image). Use for image create/modify requests incl. edits. Supports text-to-image + image-to-image; 1K/2K/4K; use --input-image.\n使用 Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image) 生成或编辑图像。支持文生图、图生图及 1K/2K/4K 分辨率，适用于图像创建、修改及编辑请求，使用 --input-image 指定输入图像。\n  - version: 1.0.1\nopenai-whisper  Openai Whisper\n  - Local speech-to-text with the Whisper CLI (no API key).\n本地语音转文字（Whisper CLI，无需 API 密钥）\n  - version: 1.0.0\nauto-updater  Auto-Updater Skill\n  - Automatically update Clawdbot and all installed skills once daily. Runs via cron, checks for updates, applies them, and messages the user with a summary of what changed.\n每日自动通过cron检查并更新Clawdbot及所有已安装技能，应用后向用户发送变更摘要。\n  - version: 1.0.0\napi-gateway  API Gateway\n  - Connect to 100+ APIs (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, GitHub, Notion, Slack, Airtable, HubSpot, etc.) with managed OAuth. Use this skill when users want to...\n通过托管OAuth连接100+ API（Google Workspace、Microsoft 365、GitHub、Notion、Slack、Airtable、HubSpot等）。当用户想要...时使用此技能。\n  - version: 1.0.69","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773998714657}}
